diff --git a/cpp/benchmarks/ndsh/VORTEX.md b/cpp/benchmarks/ndsh/VORTEX.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..88614bf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cpp/benchmarks/ndsh/VORTEX.md
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# Experimental Vortex adapter
+
+`CUDF_NDSH_WITH_VORTEX=ON` adds a local-file Parquet/Vortex comparison for Q6
+and projected reads. Default **OFF** adds no Vortex dependency. Q1 and other
+queries remain Parquet-only.
+
+## Build
+
+Use a complete local Vortex checkout with CUDA-layout edition registration,
+device decimal slicing, bitmap alignment/padding, dictionary export, and
+`vx_cuda_scan_path_arrow_device_stream_projected`. The retained pin lacks these fixes;
+publish a fixed revision before removing the local-only gate. The header-flag
+check alone does not verify all runtime fixes.
+
+From the cuDF root in a RAPIDS development environment:
+
+```sh
+cmake -S cpp -B cpp/build-vortex -G Ninja \
+  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+  -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF -DBUILD_BENCHMARKS=ON \
+  -DCUDF_NDSH_WITH_VORTEX=ON \
+  -DFETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_VORTEX=/absolute/path/to/updated/vortex \
+  -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=90
+CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4 cmake --build cpp/build-vortex \
+  --target NDSH_VORTEX_BUILD_SMOKE NDSH_VORTEX_IO_TEST \
+    NDSH_DATA_GENERATOR_TEST NDSH_Q06_NVBENCH --parallel 2
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_VORTEX_BUILD_SMOKE
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_VORTEX_IO_TEST
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_DATA_GENERATOR_TEST
+compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck --error-exitcode 99 \
+  cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_VORTEX_IO_TEST
+```
+
+Requires Linux, Rust 1.95+, libclang, CUDA, and matching cuDF headers/libraries.
+Choose your GPU architecture (`90` is Hopper). Use a consistent compiler/sysroot
+and toolkit; set `CMAKE_CUDA_COMPILER`, `CUDAToolkit_ROOT`, and Cargo's `NVCC_CCBIN`
+when needed. Check Conda's `NVCC_PREPEND_FLAGS` for conflicts.
+
+Uncached dependencies need network access. Vortex uses its own CUB/nvCOMP;
+keep the Cargo build tree intact because runtime libraries are not packaged here.
+
+## Q6 comparison
+
+```sh
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_Q06_NVBENCH \
+  --benchmark ndsh_q6_local_warm --axis scale_factor=0.01 \
+  --min-samples 3 --timeout 3 --json q6-sf001.json
+```
+
+Runs `format={parquet,vortex}` × `workload={read,q6}` on identical full lineitem
+files. Both project the same four columns; Q6 applies all filters after reading.
+Schema/values are checked against the generated input; both GPU revenues must match
+a bounded-batch CPU reference of that same table. Empty Q6 is rejected. Checks and
+writing are outside timing. Warm-page-cache timing includes result destruction and
+GPU completion. Compare CPU wall time; RMM peaks exclude Vortex allocations.
+The original `ndsh_q6` retains its host-buffer Parquet/date-pushdown path separately.
+
+**Data change:** discount uses a separate fixed RNG seed, removing Q6's zero-match
+correlation with quantity. This changes lineitem and dependent values for all NDS-H
+queries, even with Vortex OFF; regenerate fixtures. Other correlations and an existing
+price-row-ordering defect remain. Separate generations can differ, so compare formats
+using the shared fixture, not old results. `NDSH_DATA_GENERATOR_TEST` is Vortex-independent.
+
+## Contract and scope
+
+- `write_vortex`: cuDF chunks → compact host Arrow → CPU-compressed local file.
+- `read_vortex`: pinned-host staging → HtoD → GPU decode → Arrow Device import →
+  owning cuDF copies and concatenation. Dictionary compression exports as plain
+  values. **No GPUDirect Storage.**
+- Contexts are single-threaded, device 0. Caller stream/resource must outlive the
+  context and returned tables. Reads finish consumer work and temporary cleanup;
+  results outlive the context/file. See `vortex_io.hpp` for argument constraints.
+- Flat typed columns and ordered top-level projection only. No predicate pushdown,
+  remote/device-buffer sources, GPU writing, or full RMM integration. Row chunking
+  is not a byte budget; peak read memory includes batches plus the concatenated result.
+- Time the complete read, including schema export, import, copies, concatenation,
+  and GPU completion; exclude writing. Tests establish correctness, not SF100
+  readiness or performance. For profiling, use `RelWithDebInfo` and optionally
+  `NVCC_APPEND_FLAGS=-lineinfo`.
